# Public application IDs only. Never put client secrets in VITE_* variables.
# Google: enable Drive API, create a Web OAuth client, and register each site's
# JavaScript origin (including http://127.0.0.1:5180 for local development).
# Configure the consent screen for https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.appdata.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# Microsoft: register an SPA supporting personal and organizational accounts.
# Add delegated Files.ReadWrite.AppFolder permission and register the exact URI:
# https://cuberplus.com/auth-callback.html
# Also register http://127.0.0.1:5180/auth-callback.html for local development.
# If the portal rejects HTTP loopback addresses, add it to spa.redirectUris
# in the app registration's Microsoft Graph manifest instead.
# The callback must be served without Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy headers.
VITE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
# Copy to .env.local, fill in public IDs, and restart Vite (or rebuild production).
